    "body": "ok,\n\nthis is the IDL definition:\n\nattribute long tabIndex;\n\nit says there is a return object \"long\" which means integer right?\n\ntake this example:\n\n<p id=\"myP\">Paragraph</p>\n\n<a id=\"myLink\" href=\"#egal\">Link</a>\n\nvar myP = d.getElementByid('myP'),\nvar myLink = d.getElementByid('myLink');\n\nmyP.tabIndex; returns ⇒ -1 \n\nmyLink.tabIndex; returns ⇒ 0\n\neverything ok so far, but if I try this:\n\nmyP.tabIndex = 0; it works fine changing the content attribute tabindex, it woks in the browser, myP is now focusable, but the operation does not give me a return value (for example in the console).\n\nwhen I do this again:\n\nmyP.tabIndex;  returns ⇒ 0 everything is like expected, but there is no return-value on setting.\n",
